      "caption": "One verb, three shapes: <b>am</b> goes with <i>I</i>, <b>is</b> with <i>he / she / it</i>, <b>are</b> with <i>you / we / they</i>. In a question, <i>be</i> jumps in front of the person."
    },
    {
      "type": "map",
      "title": "Who goes with which shape?",
      "center": "be",
      "branches": [
        {
          "label": "am",
          "items": [
            "I am → I'm"
          ],
          "tone": "a"
        },
        {
          "label": "is",
          "items": [
            "he is → he's",
            "she is → she's",
            "it is → it's",
            "Mateo is / the dog is"
          ],
          "tone": "b"
        },
        {
          "label": "are",
          "items": [
            "you are → you're",
            "we are → we're",
            "they are → they're",
            "Sofia and Liam are"
          ],
          "tone": "c"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "How to make a question with be",
      "steps": [
        {
          "label": "Start with the statement",
          "ex": "You are eleven."
        },
        {
          "label": "Move be to the front",
          "ex": "<b>Are</b> you eleven"
        },
        {
          "label": "Add the question mark and go up with your voice",
          "ex": "Are you eleven<b>?</b>"
        }
      ],
      "caption": "No <i>do</i> is needed with <i>be</i>. <i>Be</i> makes its own questions by moving."
    }
  ],
