  "can_do": [
    "I can say my name, my age and where I am from with <i>am, is</i> and <i>are</i>.",
    "I can ask <i>Are you…?</i> / <i>Is she…?</i> and answer <i>Yes, I am</i> / <i>No, she isn't</i>.",
    "I can use the short forms <i>I'm, he's, we're</i> when I speak and write."
  ],
  "summary": [
    "<i>Be</i> has three shapes: <b>am</b> (I), <b>is</b> (he, she, it, one thing) and <b>are</b> (you, we, they, groups).",
    "Age, feelings, weather and nationality are <i>be</i> sentences: <i>I'm twelve, I'm cold, it's hot, she's Peruvian</i>.",
    "Negative: add <i>not</i> after the verb (<i>isn't, aren't, I'm not</i>).",
    "Question: move <i>be</i> to the front — <i>Are you…? Is he…?</i> — no <i>do</i> needed.",
    "Short answers use the full form: <i>Yes, I am</i>, never <i>Yes, I'm</i>."
  ]
}
